      "quantity": 1,
      "color": "Black",
      "decision": "replacement",
      "replacesStockIds": [
        "28"
      ],
      "changeReason": "D-023 (Shawn 2026-10-23: \"\u80fd\u4e0d\u80fd\u628a\u8116\u5b50\u90a3\u4e2a\u6d1e\u641e\u5927\u4e00\u70b9\u5462 \u522b\u8f6c\u675c\u90a6\u7ebf\u4e86\"; \"\u6309\u8fd9\u4e2a\u505a\uff1a\u91cd\u6253\u988c\u652f\u67b6\u548c\u5934\u5e95\u677f\u653e\u5927\u5de6\u540e\u51fa\u53e3\"): the head wires and the U20CAM cable leave the head at its left rear. The 6.4 mm gap there (between ID15, the jaw support corner walls and the screw H-jaw_support-01) becomes a vertical dia 11.0 exit at (10, 18.5) through the jaw support and the floor of the lower shell (free bore dia 6.8 with the fixed clamp half in it); the left-rear screw seat moves to (11.6, 30.2) on the pad strip behind ID15 (4.0 mm of M2.6 thread, 5.8 mm of pilot past the tip); the wall ends beside the exit are squared off so no new wall is under 1.2 mm. Jaw support: the exit cut through its left-rear corner walls and plate, the pad moved with a dia 2.8 clearance hole, and the fixed half of the two-piece wire clamp in the exit (Shawn 2026-10-23: \"\u5361\u6263\u6309\u6982\u5ff5\u56fe\"): an arc from 60 to 240 deg round the rear-left of the exit from the plate bottom to z 124.3, bore dia 7.8 with two 0.5 mm ribs, and at each end a lip over a pocket for a tongue of the loose half, with a recess for its barb. The pull from the neck goes into the jaw support.",
